$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/typescript-sdk
$type: service
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  TypeScript SDK — the Node-side counterpart to the Python SDK, targeting Mastra, Vercel AI SDK, and OpenAI Agents SDK customers. Identical token-only API surface: accept and return capability tokens and folder paths, never plaintext.

$system: smith-gray/system
name: TypeScript SDK
status: planned
type: api
runtime: node
port: 0
paths:
  - packages/sdk-typescript
depends_on:
  - cli

tech_stack:
  language: TypeScript / Node
  packaging: npm workspace package
  agent_frameworks: Mastra, Vercel AI SDK, OpenAI Agents SDK

dev:
  command: "npm test --workspace packages/sdk-typescript"
  url: ""
  env:
    SAFEKEYS_SOCKET: /run/safekeys/sidecar.sock

prod:
  url: ""
  region: ""
  deployment_ref: ""

testing:
  framework: vitest
  command: "npm test --workspace packages/sdk-typescript"
  coverage_target: "80%"

security:
  auth_method: Local sidecar socket
  secrets_ref: docs/help/security-model.md

modules:
  - name: client
    purpose: Sidecar socket client and token handling
    paths: [packages/sdk-typescript/src]

risks:
  - "Ships after the Python SDK, so API drift between the two SDKs is a risk; both must mirror the same contract."

future:
  - "Framework adapters built on top of the core SDK rather than bespoke runtimes."

decisions:
  - id: ts-after-python
    decision: Ship the TypeScript SDK immediately after the MVP, not inside it.
    rationale: The blueprint's MVP list names Python first; the TS SDK serves Node runtimes but is a second adapter on an already-proven contract, so it does not gate the two-agent demo.
    status: accepted
